relaciones:
Conditions in (1.x) are valid if the cellTechnology of the LNCEL instance is configured to 'FDD':
(1.1) actEirpControl is allowed to be configured to value not equal to 'disabled' if all of the following conditions are fulfilled:
- actPdcchLoadGen within the same parent LNCEL instance must be 'false';
- dlChBw within the same parent LNCEL instance must not be '1.4 MHz';
- dlInterferenceEnable of this cell instance must be set to 'false';
- actDynamicSharedSpectrum must be 'false';
- lteNrDssMode must be set to 'none';
- actDlPwBackoff must be set to 'false';
- actMicroDtx must be set to 'false'.
(1.2) If actMBMS is set to 'true' in the parent instance of LNBTS, actEirpControl can only be set to not equal to 'disabled' in LNCEL instances with earfcnDL in LNCEL_FDD of this cell not equal to mbsfnEarfcn in MBSFNSYNCAREA_FDD and dlChBw in same LNCEL_FDD of this cell not equal to mbsfnDlChBw in same MBSFNSYNCAREA_FDD.
(1.3) If actMBMSPS is set to 'true' in the parent instance of LNBTS, actEirpControl can only be set to not equal to 'disabled' in LNCEL instances with earfcnDL in LNCEL_FDD of this cell not equal to mbsfnEarfcn in MBSFNSYNCAREA_FDD and dlChBw in same LNCEL_FDD of this cell not equal to mbsfnDlChBw in same MBSFNSYNCAREA_FDD.
(1.4) If actEirpControl is not equal to 'disabled' then following parameters must be configured:
- eirpReduction
- antGainNonBF.

Conditions in (2.x) are valid if the cellTechnology of the LNCEL instance is configured to 'TDD':
(2.1) actEirpControl must be configured to 'disabled'.

Conditions in (3.x) are valid if the cellTechnology of the LNCEL instance is configured to 'NB-IoT-FDD':
(3.1) actEirpControl must be configured to 'disabled'.

Conditions in (1.x) are valid if the cellTechnology is configured to 'FDD' or 'TDD':
(1.1) if actTcpBoost is set to 'true', or actProactSchedBySrb is set to 'true', or ilReacTimerUl is set to a valid value other than '0', or maxNumVoLteProactUlGrantsPerTti is set to a valid value other than '0', the following is fulfilled:
- maxNumUeProactiveUl must be configured;
- maxNumUeProactiveUlNonTxSkip must be less or equal to maxNumUeProactiveUl;

Conditions in (2.x) are valid if the cellTechnology is configured to 'NB-IoT-FDD':
(2.1) maxNumUeProactiveUl must not be configured.

Conditions in (1.x) are valid if the cellTechnology is configured to 'FDD' or 'TDD':
(1.1) if actTcpBoost is set to 'true', or actProactSchedBySrb is set to 'true', or ilReacTimerUl is set to a valid value other than '0', or maxNumVoLteProactUlGrantsPerTti is set to a valid value other than '0', the following is fulfilled:
- maxNumUeProactiveUlNonTxSkip must be configured;
- maxNumUeProactiveUlNonTxSkip must be less or equal to maxNumUeProactiveUl;

Conditions in (2.x) are valid if the cellTechnology is configured to 'NB-IoT-FDD':
(2.1) maxNumUeProactiveUlNonTxSkip must not be configured.

raNondedPreamb must be equal or greater than raPreGrASize.

If actCatM is set to 'true', the following conditions must be fulfilled:
(1) raNondedPreamb + raPreGrCSizeCatM <= 64;
(2) if ulChBw is set to '5 MHz', raPreGrASize must be equal to raNondedPreamb;

(3) If numCELevelCatM is set to '2', then raNondedPreamb + raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel1-raPreGrCSizeCatM <= 64;
(4) If numCELevelCatM is set to '3', then raNondedPreamb + raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel1-raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel2-raPreGrCSizeCatM<= 64;
(5) If numCELevelCatM is set to '4', then raNondedPreamb + raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel1-raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel2-raPreGrCSizeCatM + catMCELevel3-raPreGrCSizeCatM<= 64;

If actExtCellHs is set to 'true', raNondedPreamb must be set to 4

